      "description": "Unsaved settings edits are guarded only by Settings Dialog.onClose. Internal project rename/remove, draft/history opening and native-terminal navigation invoke parent callbacks directly and can replace/unmount Settings with dirty provider/profile/extension/remote fields still present. The extension project selector also remounts its keyed child editors immediately, dropping unprepared skill/plugin/sharing edits without confirmation.",
      "locations": [
        "web/components/Settings.tsx:98",
        "web/components/Settings.tsx:143",
        "web/components/Settings.tsx:150",
        "web/components/Settings.tsx:187",
        "web/components/ExtensionsPanel.tsx:54",
        "web/Workspace.tsx:597",
        "web/Workspace.tsx:1691"
      ],
      "reproduction": "Edit a non-secret provider field, visit Project directories, then choose Rename or Remove: the sidebar-management modal replaces Settings without its existing discard prompt. Separately enter unsaved skill text and change the extension project: the keyed editor unmounts and the text is lost. Existing extension-mcp-drafts test confirms the latter clearing behavior; it does not test consent before clearing.",
      "recommendation": "Route user-driven exits through one dirty-edit guard that retains the exact pending destination. For project-scope changes, require discard consent or retain edits under their original owner; never reuse values or authorization across project boundaries. Keep existing deliberate secret/approval invalidation on hide and identity changes.",
      "validation": "Source-level control-flow trace of Settings draft registry, callbacks, Workspace modal transitions and keyed extension children. No live service or new automated test was run in this frozen audit."
    }
